From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hendra Manudinata <manoedinata@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 16:58:08 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 098/105] net: wireless: scsc: port the downstream SCSC WLAN
 driver (WLBT)

The Galaxy J4's 3.18 SCSC WLAN driver (FAPI, fullmac cfg80211) for the
Exynos7570's WLBT, on top of the SCSC maxwell core, from the
J400FXXS9CVE4 kernel. It is built against a current cfg80211, the
mac80211 backports 6.18 of OpenWrt (whose kernel has no in-tree
CFG80211), the way OpenWrt builds mt76.

Changes against downstream:
- compat.h (force-included): the ieee80211_band -> nl80211_band rename,
  STATION_INFO_* as BIT_ULL(NL80211_STA_INFO_*), slsi_scan_done() for
  cfg80211_scan_info, from_timer()
- cfg80211 op adapters for the current signatures (link_id, radio_idx,
  vif_params flags, cfg80211_ap_update, sched scan reqid);
  mgmt_frame_register (a no-op) dropped; max_sched_scan_reqs instead of
  WIPHY_FLAG_SUPPORTS_SCHED_SCAN; cfg80211_roam_info, the
  ch_switch_notify link_id, the disconnected locally_generated flag,
  the vendor event wdev
- dynamic netdevs (add/del_virtual_intf and the Android ioctl) are
  (un)registered with cfg80211_(un)register_netdevice() under the wiphy
  lock; the cfg80211 netdev notifier would take it again otherwise
- timer_setup(), proc_ops, needs_free_netdev, eth_hw_addr_set(),
  netif_trans_update(), netif_rx(), select_queue sb_dev, qdisc access
  through the qdisc ops, kref_read(), class_create(), kernel_read(),
  ktime_get_boottime_ts64(), strncasecmp()
- the MAC address fallback is random instead of the SoC unique id
- builds without warnings with GCC and CONFIG_WERROR
- GSCAN, KIC, NCHO and key management offload (Android) are left off

Tested on the J4 under OpenWrt: the driver registers phy0 (wlan0, p2p0),
the firmware starts on wlan0 up, the MAC comes from /efs/wifi/.mac.info
and a scan lists the APs around. Known issue: netifd deleting wlan0
(it replaces the interfaces of a phy) leaves a NULL netdev that the RX
path dereferences.
